      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A clinical, electrocardiographic and coronarographic study of ten cases shows that surelevation of ST-segment during exercise (without any signs of infarction) correspond to very different clinical situations of anatomical state of coronary vessels, occurrence of coronary spasm and evolution of the ischemic disease. \"Inversed coronary Insufficiency\" is proposed to design this syndrome. Practical recommandations are formulated."},
